meta {
  name: Silence Alert Rule
  type: http
  seq: 10
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/alerts/{{alert_id}}/silence
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

body:json {
  {
    "duration_secs": 7200
  }
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{jwt_token}}
}

docs {
  Temporarily mute Fired notifications for one rule. The evaluator keeps
  running: state transitions still happen, fired/resolved rows still get
  written to alert_events (with `notified: false` while silenced), and
  Resolved push notifications still go through — recovery is never
  silenced. Channel-agnostic: gates FCM, WebPush, and any other channel
  at the same point.

  Body shape:
    duration_secs — required, seconds from now. Range: 1..2592000 (30 days).

  Versus disable (`PATCH /alerts/{id}` with `enabled: false`): silence
  keeps the rule evaluating and writing history; disable stops it
  entirely. Use silence for maintenance windows and known-temporary
  noise; use disable for "stop checking this for now."

  Versus cooldown (`cooldown_secs`): cooldown is post-fire backoff and
  doesn't suppress the first fire; silence is operator-initiated and
  blocks all fires within the window.

  Response: 200 OK with the updated AlertRuleDto (echo includes the new
  `silenced_until` unix timestamp).

  Errors:
    400 BAD_REQUEST — duration out of range
    404 NOT_FOUND   — no such rule
}
